{"content_hash": "8216324dd97d075c", "version_id": 595, "article_id": 60, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Indonesia frees eight orangutans after Borneo wildfires", "title_zh": "婆罗洲大火后，印尼放归八只红毛猩猩", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "bbc_science", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6073z5rvrk3o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586778538929-ee34a8e9d8e7?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8d2F0Y2glMjBlbmRhbmdlcmVkJTIwb3Jhbmd1dGFuc3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNzY1NzczfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Dan Dennis on Unsplash", "author": "Dan Dennis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@cameramandan83?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/brown-monkey-on-brown-wooden-log-during-daytime-5ESfIy0yjZY?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(180, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(218, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "459c4da79085"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 244, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Eight critically endangered orangutans have been released into a Bornean reserve after being rescued from wildfires that ravaged their habitat. The release marks a tentative step in Indonesia's efforts to protect one of the world's most threatened apes.", "lead_zh": "八只极度濒危的红毛猩猩在从烧毁栖息地的野火中被救出后，已被放归婆罗洲的一处保护区。这次放归标志着印尼保护世界上最受威胁的猿类之一的初步努力。", "preview": "Indonesian wildlife authorities have released eight orangutans into a reserve in western Borneo, following their rescue from intense wildfir", "preview_zh": "印尼野生动物管理部门已将八只红毛猩猩放归婆罗洲西部的保护区，此前它们从席卷该岛森林的猛烈野火中被救出。这群猩猩包括三位母亲、各自带着一只女儿，以及两只成年雄性。放归于周五进行，距八月和九月大火烧毁它们的栖息地仅一个多月。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 584, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/60/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 96.7, "size_bytes": 583920, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 272, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0c12f88/content/data/versions/595.json", "paragraphs": ["Indonesian wildlife authorities have released eight orangutans into a reserve in western Borneo, following their rescue from intense wildfires that swept through the island's forests. The group comprised three mothers, each accompanied by a daughter, and two adult males. The release took place on Friday, a little over a month after fires tore through the apes' habitat in August and September.", "In total, 46 of the critically endangered apes were rescued by authorities before the flames consumed their forest home. The scale of the operation underscores the mounting pressure on Borneo's wildlife as fires, often linked to land clearing, encroach ever further on fragile ecosystems. For a species already teetering on the brink of extinction, each rescued individual represents a hard-won victory.", "Yet the release of a mere eight animals, however symbolic, lays bare the limitations of such interventions. Conservationists caution that without addressing the root causes of the fires, which destroy vast swathes of rainforest, the future of the orangutan remains precarious. The apes now face the challenge of adapting to a reserve that, while safer, is a far cry from the undisturbed wilderness they once inhabited.", "Indonesian authorities have pledged to continue monitoring the released orangutans, though questions linger over whether the reserve can sustain them in the long term. As the fires recede, the plight of these animals serves as a stark reminder of the delicate balance between human activity and biodiversity in one of the world's most biologically rich regions."], "paragraphs_zh": ["印尼野生动物管理部门已将八只红毛猩猩放归婆罗洲西部的保护区，此前它们从席卷该岛森林的猛烈野火中被救出。这群猩猩包括三位母亲、各自带着一只女儿，以及两只成年雄性。放归于周五进行，距八月和九月大火烧毁它们的栖息地仅一个多月。", "总计有46只极度濒危的红毛猩猩在火焰吞噬其森林家园前被当局救出。此次行动的规模凸显了婆罗洲野生动物面临的日益增大的压力，因为往往与土地清理相关的火灾正不断侵入脆弱的生态系统。对于一个已濒临灭绝的物种而言，每一只获救的个体都代表着一场来之不易的胜利。", "然而，仅仅放归八只动物，无论多么具有象征意义，都暴露了此类干预措施的局限性。环保人士警告称，若不解决火灾的根本原因——火灾摧毁了大片雨林——红毛猩猩的未来依然岌岌可危。这些猩猩现在面临着适应保护区的挑战，尽管保护区更安全，但远非它们曾经栖息的未受干扰的荒野。", "印尼当局承诺将继续监测放归的红毛猩猩，但保护区能否长期维持它们的生存仍存疑问。随着大火退去，这些动物的困境严峻地提醒人们，在这个世界上生物资源最丰富的地区之一，人类活动与生物多样性之间存在着微妙的平衡。"], "body": "Indonesian wildlife authorities have released eight orangutans into a reserve in western Borneo, following their rescue from intense wildfires that swept through the island's forests. The group comprised three mothers, each accompanied by a daughter, and two adult males. The release took place on Friday, a little over a month after fires tore through the apes' habitat in August and September.\n\nIn total, 46 of the critically endangered apes were rescued by authorities before the flames consumed their forest home. The scale of the operation underscores the mounting pressure on Borneo's wildlife as fires, often linked to land clearing, encroach ever further on fragile ecosystems. For a species already teetering on the brink of extinction, each rescued individual represents a hard-won victory.\n\nYet the release of a mere eight animals, however symbolic, lays bare the limitations of such interventions. Conservationists caution that without addressing the root causes of the fires, which destroy vast swathes of rainforest, the future of the orangutan remains precarious. The apes now face the challenge of adapting to a reserve that, while safer, is a far cry from the undisturbed wilderness they once inhabited.\n\nIndonesian authorities have pledged to continue monitoring the released orangutans, though questions linger over whether the reserve can sustain them in the long term. As the fires recede, the plight of these animals serves as a stark reminder of the delicate balance between human activity and biodiversity in one of the world's most biologically rich regions.", "body_zh": "印尼野生动物管理部门已将八只红毛猩猩放归婆罗洲西部的保护区，此前它们从席卷该岛森林的猛烈野火中被救出。这群猩猩包括三位母亲、各自带着一只女儿，以及两只成年雄性。放归于周五进行，距八月和九月大火烧毁它们的栖息地仅一个多月。\n\n总计有46只极度濒危的红毛猩猩在火焰吞噬其森林家园前被当局救出。此次行动的规模凸显了婆罗洲野生动物面临的日益增大的压力，因为往往与土地清理相关的火灾正不断侵入脆弱的生态系统。对于一个已濒临灭绝的物种而言，每一只获救的个体都代表着一场来之不易的胜利。\n\n然而，仅仅放归八只动物，无论多么具有象征意义，都暴露了此类干预措施的局限性。环保人士警告称，若不解决火灾的根本原因——火灾摧毁了大片雨林——红毛猩猩的未来依然岌岌可危。这些猩猩现在面临着适应保护区的挑战，尽管保护区更安全，但远非它们曾经栖息的未受干扰的荒野。\n\n印尼当局承诺将继续监测放归的红毛猩猩，但保护区能否长期维持它们的生存仍存疑问。随着大火退去，这些动物的困境严峻地提醒人们，在这个世界上生物资源最丰富的地区之一，人类活动与生物多样性之间存在着微妙的平衡。", "text": "Indonesian wildlife authorities have released eight orangutans into a reserve in western Borneo, following their rescue from intense wildfires that swept through the island's forests. The group comprised three mothers, each accompanied by a daughter, and two adult males. The release took place on Friday, a little over a month after fires tore through the apes' habitat in August and September. In total, 46 of the critically endangered apes were rescued by authorities before the flames consumed their forest home. The scale of the operation underscores the mounting pressure on Borneo's wildlife as fires, often linked to land clearing, encroach ever further on fragile ecosystems. For a species already teetering on the brink of extinction, each rescued individual represents a hard-won victory. Yet the release of a mere eight animals, however symbolic, lays bare the limitations of such interventions. Conservationists caution that without addressing the root causes of the fires, which destroy vast swathes of rainforest, the future of the orangutan remains precarious. The apes now face the challenge of adapting to a reserve that, while safer, is a far cry from the undisturbed wilderness they once inhabited. Indonesian authorities have pledged to continue monitoring the released orangutans, though questions linger over whether the reserve can sustain them in the long term. As the fires recede, the plight of these animals serves as a stark reminder of the delicate balance between human activity and biodiversity in one of the world's most biologically rich regions.", "vocab": [{"word": "critically endangered", "pos": "adj", "zh": "极度濒危的", "note": "用于描述物种面临极高灭绝风险", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ravage", "pos": "verb", "zh": "毁坏，蹂躏", "note": "常指火灾、战争等造成严重破坏", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "comprise", "pos": "verb", "zh": "由……组成", "note": "较正式，相当于 consist of", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "underscore", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强调，凸显", "note": "新闻用语，表示突出重要性", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "encroach", "pos": "verb", "zh": "侵占，蚕食", "note": "常与 on/upon 连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "teeter on the brink of", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "濒临……边缘", "note": "形象表达，常用于危机情境", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "hard-won", "pos": "adj", "zh": "来之不易的", "note": "强调经过努力才获得", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lay bare", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "暴露，揭示", "note": "常用于揭露问题或真相", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "precarious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不稳定的，危险的", "note": "形容局势或状态岌岌可危", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "a far cry from", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "与……大相径庭", "note": "表示差距很大", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pledge", "pos": "verb", "zh": "承诺，保证", "note": "正式承诺做某事", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "linger", "pos": "verb", "zh": "持续存在，萦绕", "note": "指问题、疑问等迟迟不消失", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "plight", "pos": "noun", "zh": "困境，苦难", "note": "常指不幸的处境", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "biodiversity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "生物多样性", "note": "生态学常用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires", "summary_original": "The critically endangered apes were rescued from intense wildfires that destroyed their habitat in August and September.", "body_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nTo play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser.\nThis video can not be played\nWatch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nClose\nEight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires.\nThree mothers, their three daughters and two adult males were freed in a reserve in the west of the island on Friday.\nIndonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 of the apes, which are critically endangered, before fires tore through their habitat in August and September.\nRead more on this story.\nSubsection\nAsia\nPublished\n50 minutes ago\nShare\nclose panel\nShare page\nCopy link\nAbout sharing\nRelated topics\nIndonesia\nFollow\nIndonesia\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nIndonesia\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nOrangutans\nFollow\nOrangutans\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nOrangutans\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nBorneo\nFollow\nBorneo\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nBorneo\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nConservation\nFollow\nConservation\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nConservation\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nWildfires\nFollow\nWildfires\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nWildfires\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nRead description", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:42:52.124893", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Indonesian", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.737, "sm": 100, "em": 737, "cs": 0, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "wildlife", "s": 0.75, "e": 1.288, "sm": 750, "em": 1287, "cs": 11, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "authorities", "s": 1.3, "e": 1.863, "sm": 1300, "em": 1862, "cs": 20, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "have", "s": 1.875, "e": 2.05, "sm": 1875, "em": 2050, "cs": 32, "ce": 36, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "released", "s": 2.062, "e": 2.525, "sm": 2062, "em": 2525, "cs": 37